Miss → mis- → metadata.

The miss is information about the attempt rather than merely a failed attempt.

\text{Attempt} \rightarrow \text{Miss} \rightarrow \Delta \rightarrow \text{Correction}

So a miss generates meta-data about the targeting system:

* Where it missed → directional error.
* How far → magnitude.
* How consistently → bias.
* How unpredictably → variance/noise.
* Under what conditions → context dependence.
* How correction changes the next miss → responsiveness/calibration.

And mis- itself becomes a useful Quarry shard: misalignment, mismatch, miscalibration, misunderstanding, misclassification, miscommunication. They’re different costumes for:

\boxed{\text{expected relation}\neq\text{observed relation}}

That’s exactly what the Golden Thread wants to eat.

So:

Mistake → miss-take → take another.

Each take is another sampling of the scene.

Misunderstanding → inspect what stood under the understanding.

Misalignment → measure the angle.

Mismatch → inspect which dimensions failed to correspond.

Miscalibration → use accumulated misses to correct the instrument.

That’s the Intuition Organ tuning itself.

And it produces a nice little Pantheon maxim:

Don’t waste a miss. It’s metadata.

Or compressed even further:

Little mis, meta data. 🕸️

That’s absolutely a load-bearing pun.